# Examples with artifacts and dependencies:

## Example 1 (Python project with build artifacts):
```
### Added files:
['__pycache__/main.cpython-39.pyc', 'dist/app.js', 'build/lib/main.class', 'node_modules/lodash/index.js', '.env.local', '.vscode/settings.json', 'temp_file.tmp', 'app.log']

### Deleted files:
['old_module.py']

### Modified files:
['src/main.py', 'requirements.txt']

### current .gitignore Content
'*.log'
```

Output:
```
# Compiled and binary files
*.pyc
__pycache__/
*.class
*.o
*.obj
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.a
*.out

# Build artifacts
dist/
build/

# Dependencies
node_modules/
venv/
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
pip-wheel-metadata/

# Logs and temp files
*.log
*.tmp
*.swp
*.swo

# Environment files
.env
.env.local
*.env.*

# Editors and IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Original rules preserved
*.log
```

## Example 2 (JavaScript/Node project):
```
### Added files:
['node_modules/react/package.json', 'dist/bundle.js', 'build/static/css/main.css', '.npmrc', '.vscode/launch.json', 'package-lock.json', '.env.production']

### Deleted files:
[]

### Modified files:
['src/App.js', 'package.json']

### current .gitignore Content
'node_modules/'
```

Output:
```
# Dependencies
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Build artifacts
dist/
build/
*.min.js
*.min.css

# Environment
.env
*.env.*

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Original rules preserved
node_modules/
```

## Example 3 (Java/Maven project):
```
### Added files:
['target/classes/Main.class', 'target/test-classes/TestMain.class', '.gradle/caches/modules-2/files-2.1/junit/junit/4.13.2/', 'build/libs/my-app.jar', '.idea/workspace.xml', 'out/production/classes/MyClass.class']

### Deleted files:
[]

### Modified files:
['src/main/java/com/example/Main.java', 'pom.xml']

### current .gitignore Content
'target/'
```

Output:
```
# Compiled files
*.class
*.jar
*.war
*.ear

# Build artifacts
target/
build/
out/

# Dependencies and caches
.gradle/
.gradle-wrapper/

# IDE
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws

# Original rules preserved
target/
```

## Example 4 (Go project):
```
### Added files:
['vendor/github.com/some/package/file.go', 'bin/app', 'go.sum', 'go.mod', '.vscode/settings.json', 'coverage.out']

### Deleted files:
[]

### Modified files:
['main.go', 'go.mod']

### current .gitignore Content
''
```

Output:
```
# Binaries
bin/
*.exe
*.out
*.test

# Dependencies
vendor/

# Coverage
coverage.out

# Editors
.vscode/
*.swp

# Go-specific
*.o
*.a
```

## Example 5 (Python project with virtual env):
```
### Added files:
['venv/bin/python', 'venv/lib/python3.9/site-packages/requests/__init__.py', '__pycache__/utils.cpython-39.pyc', '.pytest_cache/v/cache/nodeids', 'htmlcov/index.html', 'docs/_build/html/index.html', '.env.test']

### Deleted files:
[]

### Modified files:
['src/utils.py', 'tests/test_utils.py']

### current .gitignore Content
'__pycache__/'
```

Output:
```
# Virtual environments
venv/
.venv/
env/

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python

# Testing
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.nox/
.tox/

# Environment
.env
*.env.*

# Build docs
docs/_build/

# Original rules preserved
__pycache__/
```

## Example 6 (C++ project):
```
### Added files:
['build/CMakeFiles/CMakeDirectoryInformation.cmake', 'bin/myapp.exe', 'obj/src/main.o', '.vscode/tasks.json', 'core', 'cmake-build-debug/CMakeCache.txt']

### Deleted files:
[]

### Modified files:
['src/main.cpp', 'CMakeLists.txt']

### current .gitignore Content
'build/'
```

Output:
```
# Build artifacts
build/
cmake-build-*/
bin/
obj/
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.exe
*.out

# Debug and core dumps
core
*.stackdump

# Editors
.vscode/
*.swp

# Original rules preserved
build/
```

## Example 7 (Rust project):
```
### Added files:
['target/debug/deps/my_app-1234567890abcdef.d', 'target/release/my_app', 'Cargo.lock', '.cargo/config.toml', 'target/.rustc_info.json', '.vscode/settings.json']

### Deleted files:
[]

### Modified files:
['src/main.rs', 'Cargo.toml']

### current .gitignore Content
'target/'
```

Output:
```
# Build artifacts
target/

# Cargo lock file (if not intended to be committed)
Cargo.lock

# Editors
.vscode/
*.swp

# Original rules preserved
target/
```

## Example 8 (Just source files - no artifacts):
```
### Added files:
['src/main.py', 'README.md', 'config.json', 'src/utils.py']

### Deleted files:
['old_file.txt']

### Modified files:
['requirements.txt', 'src/main.py']

### current .gitignore Content
''
```

Output:
```
# No output (empty - only source/config files)
```